Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.60,0:00:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.42,0:00:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This girl is Jolyne Kujo, but where\Nin God's name is Lang Wrangler?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.36,0:00:23.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I right to assume that\Nhe failed his objective
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.88,0:00:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,and she still has the\Ndisc in her possession?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,If so, within a few moments,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.92,0:00:31.06,Default,,0,0,0,,she will meet someone at the courtyard\Nand hand the disc off to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.14,0:00:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.50,0:00:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,He serves as a priest\Nat the prison's chapel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.68,0:00:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What is he doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.86,0:00:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Did she find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.92,0:00:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.83,0:00:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If she had any inkling\Nthat I was her enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.52,0:00:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,we would be in the midst\Nof battle right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.42,0:00:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on! Father, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.36,0:00:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg of you, whatever you do,\Nplease don't sound that alarm!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.94,0:00:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The last thing that I want here is to\Ncause trouble or make some kind of scene!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.52,0:00:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.80,0:00:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Should I take the chance\Nand knock him out?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.00,0:01:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure I could, if it's to\Nbring my old man back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.12,0:01:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Hitting a priest is nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.48,0:01:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you ignoring the\Nreal problem happening here?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.42,0:01:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You've taken someone else's work permit\Ncard and used it to get me to open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.60,0:01:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Pray tell what has become of the\Nprisoner this card actually belongs to,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.70,0:01:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Lang Wrangler.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.20,0:01:23.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you just met me, so I won't\Nask you to believe what I'm saying.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.52,0:01:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But I have no reason\Nto lie to you, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.82,0:01:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I was assaulted by the prisoner you're\Nreferring to, so I defended myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.60,0:01:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He's in that hamper probably dreaming\Nabout how I knocked him out cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.46,0:01:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Regardless of the reason, I am obligated\Nto report this matter to the authorities.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.86,0:01:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, do what you have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.76,0:01:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,However, it has to be after\NI get to the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.96,0:01:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me two minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.38,0:01:47.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, all I need is a single\Nsolitary minute, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.90,0:01:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me go to the courtyard\Nand you can turn me in.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.38,0:01:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all I ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.78,0:01:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you asking me to\Noverlook your wrongdoings?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.32,0:01:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone's life is on the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.94,0:02:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,My own dad's life and spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.50,0:02:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Surely a priest like yourself\Ncan understand my situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.68,0:02:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you by your lonesome?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.46,0:02:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Or is there anyone else in here with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:10.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuh-uh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.92,0:02:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It's only me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.64,0:02:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe I just lied to a priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.30,0:02:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But a tiny lie like that can be forgiven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.90,0:02:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and mentioning the disks would\Nsend up immediate red flags.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.02,0:02:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Father, one minute is all I ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.78,0:02:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,In most cases, when someone\Ndoes something for others,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.82,0:02:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,they expect to receive some\Nsort of reward in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.20,0:02:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,To be kind to others is to expect that\Nsame kindness from those you give it to,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.98,0:02:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and that cannot be called\Nunconditional love.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.70,0:02:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,True unconditional love, my dear,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.04,0:02:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,is the reward of eventually\Nreaching the gates of heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.82,0:02:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You may go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.84,0:02:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I will pretend that our\Npaths never crossed here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.40,0:02:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But per your request,\Nyou only have one minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.42,0:02:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I trust you'll return to this gate\Nby then and not a second longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.20,0:03:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I had to let her go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.16,0:03:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Despite her lie, I know\Nsomeone is hiding there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.42,0:03:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,If she does have comrades around,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.28,0:03:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot risk revealing\Nthat I am Palesnake's user.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.12,0:03:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,even if it is to dispose of Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.48,0:03:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,According to the Speedwagon Foundation,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.76,0:03:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll know how to hand over the disc\Nonce I arrive at the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.06,0:03:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess this is what they meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.88,0:03:37.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.79,0:03:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have a pass that\Npermits you to be out here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.16,0:03:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna say that's a no.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So that must mean you're trying to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.98,0:03:53.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.89,0:03:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.78,0:03:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounding the alarm was\Nnever part of my plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.02,0:04:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad I thought ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.06,0:04:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Having a guard patrol the\Ncourtyard was the perfect decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.56,0:04:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.84,0:04:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.75,0:04:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not enough to go to the party.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.84,0:04:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Get away!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.96,0:04:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not enough, I'm not enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.14,0:04:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not enough, I'm not enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.76,0:05:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Break out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.42,0:05:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not enough, but I'm close.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.52,0:05:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Break out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.56,0:05:14.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.92,0:05:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,stop
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.74,0:05:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,beating!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.65,0:05:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't stop beating!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.88,0:05:31.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't stop beating! I'm out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.12,0:05:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,In the year 1988, my life took a turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.72,0:05:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I met a man from Egypt who possessed\Nthe ability to stop time itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.98,0:05:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and we developed a rather\Nclose relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.42,0:05:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,One evening, he suddenly told me this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.52,0:06:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,If someone wished to go to\Nheaven, there may be a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.70,0:06:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He was young and unbelievably beautiful,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:09.06,Default,,0,0,0,,but with an aura about him that suggested\Nhe had lived for hundreds of years.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.14,0:06:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,At that time, I was 16, and a\Nstudent aspiring to go to a seminary.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.46,0:06:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, don't look at me that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.76,0:06:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just talking about the human mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.96,0:06:22.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not like I'm telling\Nyou to wither and die.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.48,0:06:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,This heaven pertains to our spirits,\Nand where they go after death.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.40,0:06:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,As your spirit evolves,\Nso too does your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.42,0:06:32.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Where they ultimately end\Nup is what fascinates me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.86,0:06:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Surely you, of all people,\Nunderstand what I'm talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.94,0:06:39.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It's there that one will\Nfind true happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.96,0:06:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That is, if they can make\Nit into heaven, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.20,0:06:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Though I'm aware, joy cannot be\Nfound by having an invincible body,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.40,0:06:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,vast riches, or even\Nreigning over all humanity.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.76,0:06:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,In the end, the true winner is the\None who gets to witness heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.26,0:07:01.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I will get there\Nsomeday, no matter what it costs me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.14,0:07:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,And how are you going to\Nachieve that, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.30,0:07:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.94,0:07:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I wrote the process in a notebook.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.44,0:07:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,One day, find me in Egypt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.68,0:07:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll show it to you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.06,0:07:18.52,Default,,0,0,0,,If I ever hope to figure this\Nout, I will need you to assist me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.34,0:07:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,However, before I could learn\Nthe means of attaining heaven...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.38,0:07:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The notebook he spoke\Nof was burned to ash.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.92,0:07:33.68,Default,,0,0,0,,By none other than Jotaro Kujo's father.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.80,0:07:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro Kujo.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.30,0:07:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro laid eyes on the contents of the\Nnotebook that day, and with the book
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.94,0:07:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,gone, the information was sealed with him\Nforever, along with the man who aimed for
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.18,0:07:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,heaven, Dio Brando himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.92,0:07:56.36,Default,,0,0,0,,For the next 20 years, I waited patiently\Nfor my chance to obtain Jotaro's memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.64,0:08:00.17,Default,,0,0,0,,so that I could relive the\Nmoment that he read the notebook.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.44,0:08:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,And finally after decades I got it.\NHis memories were mine, along with
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.76,0:08:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The Stand that surpassed even DIO,\NStar Platinum, I ensured that Jotaro's
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.18,0:08:16.18,Default,,0,0,0,,body would wither and decay and\Nalthough his troublesome daughter
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.26,0:08:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,behaved in ways i never could have\Nexpected it's all taken care of now
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.52,0:08:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.43,0:08:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,She got shot?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.35,0:08:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene got shot? But by who? A guard?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.16,0:08:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe that bastard Pale\NSnake figured out where she was
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.94,0:08:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,going to deliver the disc and\Nhe's hiding around here somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.24,0:08:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,JOLENE!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.80,0:08:49.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The Guard and Control will take\Ncare of retrieving Star Platinum,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.02,0:08:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,So there's no reason for\Nme to stay here anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.94,0:08:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,With that out of the way, I\Nshould head back to the chapel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.02,0:08:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.93,0:09:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What was I doing out here again?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.00,0:09:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh right, the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.68,0:09:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I was given orders to bring this\Nthing back without a scratch on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.62,0:09:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,And I was also ordered to make sure\NJolene Kuja was finished off for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.54,0:09:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Thing is, I don't know\Nwho gave me these orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.58,0:09:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't seem to remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.36,0:09:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,doesn't matter either way i\Nwas given orders to completely
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.36,0:09:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,blast straight through jolene's\Nhead with this gun damn it
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.72,0:09:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,all there's nothing i can do to\Nhelp you now in your greatest
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.50,0:09:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,moment of need i'm utterly\Nuseless it's over now jolene kujo
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.34,0:10:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.04,0:10:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My weather forecast is a\Npower to control the weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.72,0:10:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,At this point, this is all I can offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.84,0:10:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, I wasn't able to save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.78,0:10:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I might be able to protect the\Ndisk, and if you still have
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.56,0:10:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,the strength within you to keep\Nfighting you may be able to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.10,0:10:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,survive between.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.72,0:10:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,the years of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.66,0:10:38.14,Default,,0,0,0,,1887 and 1974 in the state of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.22,0:10:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Florida alone there were more than 50\Nreported cases of fish, frogs, snakes,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.88,0:10:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,and sheep falling from the\Nsky in unbelievable numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.70,0:10:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It was caused by a tornado.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.86,0:10:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,At least that's what they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.58,0:10:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And these colorful amphibians\Nare poison dart frogs
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.66,0:10:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,that live on treetops in\NCentral and South America.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.70,0:11:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,They carry a deadly poison\Nunder their skin that
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.56,0:11:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Aboriginal Americans\Nused for their blowguns.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.68,0:11:22.90,Default,,0,0,0,,This is judging by the color of\Nthese frogs' skin, they're most
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.98,0:11:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,certainly poison dart frogs it\Ntakes less than a few seconds
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.18,0:11:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,for the poison to get inside\Nthe body causing the heart and
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.96,0:11:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,respiratory system to stop\Nthat's the bodily fluid that's
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.20,0:11:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Being splattered all over\Nthe place right now, but this
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.06,0:11:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,power could it be his ability\Nto control the weather weather
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.84,0:11:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,forecast he's supposed to have\Nlost his memory was he the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.80,0:11:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,one hiding behind the oil drum\NI must go where's the card key
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.26,0:12:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,These frogs are deadly, poisonous.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.94,0:12:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,So much just happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.86,0:12:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I get shot?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.58,0:12:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the wound deep?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.94,0:12:25.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Crap, not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.58,0:12:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The frog's fluid is\Nsoaking into my thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.96,0:12:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.87,0:12:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,If somebody can hear me, open the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.98,0:12:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.56,0:12:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.02,0:12:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Maintain your peace of mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.52,0:12:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What should I do at a time like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.04,0:12:44.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Two, three, five, seven,\Neleven, eleven, nine, twelve.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.12,0:12:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I must stay calm, count prime\Nnumbers to compose my thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.24,0:12:52.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Prime numbers are lonely numbers that can\Nonly be divided by one and themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.84,0:12:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It gives me courage.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.96,0:13:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,23. 28.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.24,0:13:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's 29. Damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.28,0:13:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The filthy frogs are\Nclean to my $800 pants.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.50,0:13:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast is at the laundry room.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.80,0:13:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He's too far.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.71,0:13:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't make him stop these frogs from
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.68,0:13:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,raining down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.72,0:13:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Escape is my only viable option. 41. Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.48,0:13:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.64,0:13:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The guard that was at The courtyard?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.26,0:13:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.46,0:13:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he still under my control? Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.92,0:13:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.96,0:13:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Guard, are you there?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.26,0:13:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.66,0:13:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a direct order!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.72,0:13:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I need your old father!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.46,0:13:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Please help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.26,0:13:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Please beg God to spare\Nmy soul from this hell!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.74,0:13:46.70,Default,,0,0,0,,43, 47, 53, 59.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.78,0:13:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The poison! I'm begging you\Nto the Lord to save me. Stay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.98,0:13:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,calm and listen to my voice\NI need your card key get over
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.40,0:14:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,here and give it to me quickly\Ncould I be saved if I give
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.40,0:14:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,this to you hey don't Take it out\Nwhile you're over there! You fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.56,0:14:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, father, you won't!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.84,0:14:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,67, 71.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.88,0:14:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What on earth is going on in this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.96,0:14:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,All those frogs?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.90,0:14:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.66,0:14:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir, I need you to\Nopen this gate immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.00,0:14:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, why are you here, father?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.94,0:14:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What's happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.85,0:14:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.96,0:14:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,A tornado, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.08,0:14:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Now please, just hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.60,0:14:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand. Right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.58,0:14:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,These frogs are...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.18,0:14:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you standing there for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.82,0:14:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We have another guard in\Nhere who's already fallen!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.02,0:14:44.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to open the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.44,0:14:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't mean he's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.86,0:14:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,For now, try to remain calm, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.82,0:14:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go find someone\Nwho can help right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.30,0:14:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.21,0:14:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do you think you're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.46,0:14:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,All you have to do is hit the switch\Nover here, and the gate will open!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.10,0:14:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand that, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.02,0:15:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But there may be a liability.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.56,0:15:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I need to check with my supervisor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.98,0:15:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,So, please, just calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.22,0:15:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.56,0:15:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, but I am perfectly calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.58,0:15:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The only one who isn't\Ncalm here, 73, 79, is you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.82,0:15:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you going to abandon me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back right away, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.74,0:15:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Pale Snake, take a disc from\Nmy collection and hand it to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.46,0:15:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't control all of them, but\NI can choose one to enact my will!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.56,0:15:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Explode after flying 10 meters!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.00,0:15:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a direct order!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.36,0:15:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, my eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.06,0:15:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.36,0:15:48.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Please call somebody, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.66,0:15:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I need medical attention!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.56,0:15:54.80,Default,,0,0,0,,83, 89, 97.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.16,0:15:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,If you want me, I'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.98,0:15:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Just open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.46,0:16:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You must know if I'm able to\Nleave here and call for help.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.44,0:16:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,you can get treatment right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.44,0:16:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That is what you were thinking, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.08,0:16:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,If so, why would you not make it a priority\Nto move in the direction of my voice?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.42,0:16:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.58,0:16:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The disc that contains\NShotaro Kujo Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.86,0:16:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly what should I do about it now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.78,0:16:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I took care of Jolene, but I can't\Njust leave her in the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.56,0:16:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Did the gate finally open?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.52,0:16:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Please take me with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.26,0:16:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Father? Hello? Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.68,0:16:38.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.66,0:16:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.92,0:16:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't hold back the poison anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.48,0:16:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And I dropped the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.40,0:16:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't even know where it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.22,0:17:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The rain has stopped, but\Nwhere is Jolene Kujo's?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.74,0:17:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,lifeless body if I find\Nher I should find the disc
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.82,0:17:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I was frightened there\Nfor a moment but there
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.26,0:17:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,is no way frogs can defeat\Na snake search for it
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.86,0:17:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Palesnake's range of movement\Nis barely 20 meters at best
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.00,0:17:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm running a huge risk by even\Nbeing here If someone sees me,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.76,0:17:31.74,Default,,0,0,0,,all bets are off
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.50,0:17:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But there's no other way
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.30,0:17:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The soul of a deceased criminal\Nreturns to Earth in the form of a
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.96,0:17:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,frog In the name of trying to bring\Nits companions to the land of the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.56,0:17:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,dead I have heard that in the East\Nthere are stories of a similar
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.08,0:17:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,nature but this horror is truly the\Npersonification of that proverb.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.00,0:17:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonetheless, the disc I seek\Nmust be around here somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.10,0:17:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, Pale Snake.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.66,0:18:03.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to sweep the area between where\Nyou are and the entrance to the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.94,0:18:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The guard may have taken it earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.10,0:18:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It should be in that direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.26,0:18:11.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, here it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.50,0:18:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I have retrieved the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.06,0:18:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.34,0:18:21.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for\Nyou to find where it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.56,0:18:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.48,0:18:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This is so gross.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.26,0:18:36.84,Default,,0,0,0,,They're all over my face.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.02,0:18:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Makes me want to throw up!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.56,0:18:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The poison only comes out when\Nthe frogs splatter on impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.76,0:18:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,So if they don't explode,\Nthey're harmless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.92,0:18:47.68,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I made a net using live frogs,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.92,0:18:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to lessen the impact\Nof the frogs still falling.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.44,0:18:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Which allowed me to lay in wait\Nfor you to locate the disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.10,0:18:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.38,0:19:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.70,0:19:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Accept your fate and die!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.00,0:19:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it was already here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.36,0:19:17.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The Speedwagon Foundation's\Nmessenger wasn't human.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.32,0:19:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You just didn't even see that\Nit was here right on time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.82,0:19:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Weaving through the deadly\Nrain of frogs like an angel,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.58,0:19:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,it made it to this courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.56,0:19:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Savage Guardian is the\Nname of that pigeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.58,0:19:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And like all trained carrier pigeons, it\Nwill bring the disc to its rightful place.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.56,0:19:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hail, Snake!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.66,0:19:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The gun that the guard dropped\Nearlier is still over near the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.80,0:19:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Blow that bird out of the sky!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.98,0:19:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh, idiotic guard!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.58,0:19:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He completely emptied the clip of bullets!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.70,0:19:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.00,0:19:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I won.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.68,0:19:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't underestimate me, you insolent brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.12,0:19:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,This changes nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.06,0:20:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Even with Star Platinum Return,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.84,0:20:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,your father would be nothing\Nmore than a broken puppet!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.12,0:20:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He will never be able to recognize\Nyou as his own daughter again!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.32,0:20:08.12,Default,,0,0,0,,This little game is over!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.66,0:20:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.57,0:20:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a guard knocked out over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.26,0:20:13.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't step on the guards,\Nand check the courtyard!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.06,0:20:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,There might be someone else!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.18,0:20:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No, not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.86,0:20:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't faint here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.62,0:20:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The stand user has to be nearby somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.78,0:20:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to find out who\NPale Snake really is.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.12,0:20:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And the user still has\Nmy father's memory disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.00,0:20:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now's the best chance I'm gonna\Nget to discover who they are!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.10,0:20:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.01,0:20:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Look outside the window!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.38,0:20:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh my god! Unbelievable!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.62,0:20:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a bloody miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.56,0:20:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But who's gonna clean up this mess?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.76,0:20:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing has changed at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.72,0:20:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The only reason I stole Star\NPlatinum in the first place was
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.04,0:20:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,to defeat Jotaro Kujo and avenge\Nthe death of my best friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.42,0:20:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What matters most is the memory disk,\Nand it still remains in my possession.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.06,0:21:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything is going as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.52,0:21:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The instructions on how to reach heaven\Ncan only be found in Jotaro's memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.02,0:21:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,An abnormal occurrence\Nwhere frogs rain down
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.92,0:21:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,from the sky solely in\Nthe prison courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.50,0:21:28.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Through the chaos of\Nthis unexplainable event,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.24,0:21:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene's attempt at\Nescaping went unquestioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.70,0:21:35.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to a feathered friend,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.86,0:21:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,the Speedwagon Foundation\Nobtained the disc
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.24,0:21:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,which contains Jotaro\NKujo's Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.28,0:21:46.52,Default,,0,0,0,,However, without the memory disc, Jotaro's\Nmind and soul will never be restored.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.28,0:22:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I cope
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.14,0:22:07.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My head is filled with hope
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.78,0:22:15.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Of some place other than here
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.52,0:22:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I smile
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.28,0:22:27.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside and all the while
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.08,0:22:35.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering About my destiny
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.06,0:22:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking about
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.68,0:22:50.04,Default,,0,0,0,,All the things I'd
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.12,0:22:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,like to do in my life
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.94,0:23:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a dreamer,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.40,0:23:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,a distant dreamer
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.12,0:23:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Dreaming for all
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.42,0:23:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,From today
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.96,0:23:25.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Sports Maximum This is the bone\Nthat I want to ask you about
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.18,0:23:31.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Using your unique abilities There\Nis something I would like to try
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.60,0:23:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.52,0:23:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Does that belong to a human?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.68,0:23:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Whose bone is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.88,0:23:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That answer is none of your business.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.12,0:23:41.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's just say it belongs\Nto an old friend of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.28,0:23:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The bone of my dear friend, the Great Dio.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.88,0:24:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.68,0:24:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
